# Natural grammar for the Spanish subset (Phase 2), as one would write it without thinking of LL(1)
# It has left recursion and it is ambiguous: in "el maestro lee la carta en la casa" the phrase
# "en la casa" can modify "carta" (NounPhrase -> NounPhrase PrepPhrase) or "lee"
# (VerbPhrase -> VerbPhrase PrepPhrase). Both derivations exist, so the sentence has two trees.
# It is not used by the parser: it is the starting point of the formal analysis.

Sentence -> NounPhrase VerbPhrase
NounPhrase -> DET NOUN | NounPhrase ADJ | NounPhrase PrepPhrase
VerbPhrase -> VERB | VERB NounPhrase | VerbPhrase ADV | VerbPhrase PrepPhrase
PrepPhrase -> PREP NounPhrase
